      "path": "README.md",
      "text": "# New Folk Tunes Vault\r\n\r\nYou can delete this file once you're done with it!\r\n\r\n## Next steps\r\n\r\n- Update the templates with any additional information you'd like copied into new tunes/set/composers/etc.\r\n- You can delete the same tunes, set and dots - they're just there as an example.\r\n- Add any origins, types or other metadata you'd like to use in your database.\r\n- Start populating the vault with all your tunes and sets!\r\n    - You can use the `Add Tune` command to add a new tune to the vault.\r\n    - You can use the `Add Set` command to add a new set to the vault.\r\n    - You can use the `Add Composer` command to add a new composer to the vault.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Start reviewing your tunes\r\n\r\n- On a windows machine, you can press Ctrl + P to open the command palette.\r\n- On a mobile, drag down from the top of the screen to see all options.\r\n\r\n- Type \"folk tune\" to see all available options.\r\n  - `Start Review` is a full review\r\n  - `Add review to current tune` can add review data to the currently opened tune\r\n  - `Show stats` shows some useful stats about all the tunes in your vault"
